  "body": "Reported by the maintainer (2026-11-13, in chat, on v0.19.0, in the 2D Pocket operation): \"you cannot really see edge selects the edge gets Purple ish, but its to faint and not marked enough for users to actually see it.. also there is no Ctrl or Shift selection of edges so you can only select one sometimes two, sometimes its the whole chain.. its very sporadic.. this was in the 2D pocket\"\n\nWhat happens:\n1. A selected edge is drawn in a faint purple, thin line. On the shaded model it is hard to tell which edges are selected.\n2. Picking edges is unpredictable. The page hint says \"Ctrl+click adds an edge · Shift+click picks the whole loop\", but in 2D Pocket a click sometimes selects one edge, sometimes two, sometimes the whole chain, and Ctrl and Shift do not behave as the hint says.\n\nExpected:\n- Selected edges are clearly marked: a thick line in a strong selection colour that stands out on the shaded and the wireframe model in both themes, drawn over the model; the edge under the pointer has its own hover mark before the click.\n- One rule for edge picking, the same in every operation that takes edges: click selects that one edge and replaces the selection; Ctrl+click adds or removes one edge; Shift+click selects the whole loop or tangent chain of that edge. The hint text matches what happens.\n- The selection list on the Geometry page shows exactly what is selected after each click.\n\nTo find first: why the same click gives one edge, two edges or a chain (pick tolerance taking a neighbour edge, automatic chaining, or the modifier keys not reaching the pick), and whether it is 2D Pocket only or every edge-picking operation.\n\nEach selection change goes through the selection command (Everything Is a Command), so undo restores the previous selection.\n\nDone means: ui tests through the test harness pin click, Ctrl+click and Shift+click on a model with touching edges, in 2D Pocket and one other edge-picking operation, each giving the stated selection every time; the selected and hovered edge styles are named constants covered by the structural test; before and after screenshots in the PR.\n",
